{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1192960-blood-magic-vs-supernal-magic","id":1192960,"title":"Blood Magic vs Supernal Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-07T21:40:47-08:00","id":1192960,"title":"Blood Magic vs Supernal Magic","content":"Mechanically speaking, updating Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies to 2e as the sidebar (pg. 151) suggests, how well does 2e blood sorcery compare with the magic of mages?<br /> <br /> \u200bLore-wise, do blood sorcerers and &quot;true&quot; wizards have anything in common to talk about, share or perhaps work together on some obscure occult matters?<br /> <br /> \u200bTo clarify: I'm looking more at the open-ended dynamic/creative spellcasting systems of both games. Arcana and Themes.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: Perhaps I should have put this in the Awakening subforum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","user":"Rathford","date":". 03-08-2018, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T22:07:37-08:00","id":1192968,"title":"","content":"Dunno about mechanics, but lore-wise, blood sorcerers will often be harrassed by Awakened ones trying to pry into how the bloody things work (pun intended). Mages, after all, are the closest thing official material has to Mad Scientists (other than the alchemists from Promethean).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T22:24:58-08:00","id":1192973,"title":"","content":"In comparison blood magic will be flashier and more potent, without the limitation sustained spells and is technically more powerful than awakened magic... until the mage hits gnosis 3-4 at which point the mage will likely turn the vampire inside out, likewise awakened magic is SIGNIFICANTLY more flexible and less predictable than blood magic and (as of 2e) faster as blood magic in 2e can't be cast on anything less than a scale of several minutes to hours. Even without that rule, there are significant limitations to what blood sorcery can attempt compared to even a single arcana. Basically a Blood mage is about as powerful as a Life specialized mage as the two can accomplish most of the same magics, mages simply have more ability to move beyond those limits, however casting spells in one turn is a pain in the ass due to penalties that usually take multiple turns to negate while disciplines have no such penalty. In short Awakened magic trumps blood magic past the apprentice tier but a cunning vampire can still overpower a mage if they don't play fair (and when do vampires ever play fair).<br /> <br /> As to commonalities well the short answer is yes in a general sense but no in a more direct sense. Vampires would gain less from this interaction though hanging out with like minded mages who share their religious beliefs (primarily Obrimos Mysterium for the sanctum and Thrysus free council for the circle) may provide inspiration for new spells and could lead to new bloodlines. Mages gain experience for solving mysteries related to magic so they'd be all over this. However, there are no specific benefits beyond academic and scholarly interest (besides the norm of becoming a ghoul [some arcana could prevent blood binding with prep] or founding new legacies) for mages as vampire magic is apart of the fallen world. Both sides should open with non-aggressive shows of force though if they don't want the other side to start bossing them around.<br /> <br /> Basically to make this really work in either a crossover group or mixed NPCs/Antagonists develop a unique bloodline and legacy to represent the combined coven's powers working in synch (likely this would give mage sight abilities to the bloodline and allow incorporating vitae into spells as a ghoul while preventing blood bond if the vitae is consumed ritualistically). It would be very powerful but likely to earn the ire of both sides factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}